A||||6||TheFiero64||Where do I Mount the wing?||||5||
Z||000000||TheFiero64||04-26-2000||02:36 PM||||I Just got the factory wing for my Fiero notchback <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> & I want to know the factory location to mount it. Dose someone have the measurements for it? I thank you for any help you can give. Josh||||reg||5
Z||000001||batboy||04-26-2000||03:08 PM||||The usual place to mount them is on the rear deck lid...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||TheFiero64||04-26-2000||03:18 PM||||Very funny. lol  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000003||mrfixit58||04-26-2000||04:41 PM||||I just mounted one this weekend on my... uh.. my bro-in-law's, 87 GT. There were two depressions in the rib on the bottom side of the deck lid. These corresponded to the back two wing studs. I drilled holes through the deck in the center of these holes then used the gasket as a templete to drill the other two holes. Measure from the deck lid's side edges on each side to make sure the marks are square before you drill the second set of holes. This procedure will only apply if the rib in the regular lid is the same as the GT.<P>Good Luck,<BR>Roy||||reg||1
Z||000004||TOM||04-26-2000||08:49 PM||||You will also need the heavy decklid springs||||reg||1
Z||000005||TheFiero64||04-27-2000||10:57 AM||||I wish my 88 had the indentations like my GT  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> the bottom is completely smooth I can just mount it close but I like to be exact I can center it ok but Im not sure how far in to Place it?||||reg||1
Z||000006||Monkeyman||04-27-2000||06:53 PM||||Precisely 17.4376 ft from the rearmost edge of the car.  Or, depending on how frustrated you tend to get, as close to the beer cooler as possible.||||reg||1
